course: dictionary
lesson: 7258
title: Piglet: a baby pig and a famous friend
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A piglet is a baby pig. «A mother pig, called a sow, usually has about 8 to 14 piglets» at one time. The sentence tells you the sow is the mother and the piglets are her young.
explain: Look for clues about drinking and feeding. «Each piglet picks its own teat and goes back to it every feed.» Teat and feed tell you that piglets drink their mother's milk, just like other baby animals.
explain: Piglet can also be a name. In the Winnie-the-Pooh stories, Piglet is a small, shy pink pig and Pooh's friend. To tell which meaning is meant, read the words around it: «a litter of piglets» means baby pigs, but a capital P used as a name, next to Pooh, means the character.
fact: A piglet is a baby pig.
fact: «A litter of piglets» means a group of young pigs born together to one mother.
fact: A sow is a mother pig.
fact: «The runt of the litter» means the smallest piglet.
fact: Piglet is also the name of a character in Winnie-the-Pooh: a small, shy pink pig who is Pooh's anxious but brave friend.
exercise: A mother pig is called a sow. What is her baby called? | Cub | *Piglet | Kid | Calf
exercise: «A sow, a mother pig, can have a litter of a dozen piglets or more born together.» What does litter mean here? | A mess on the floor | A kind of farm gate | *A group of young born together to one mother | A small bed of straw
exercise: In the Winnie-the-Pooh stories, who is Pooh's small, shy pink friend? | Eeyore | Owl | *Piglet | Tigger
test: «Each piglet picks its own teat and goes back to it every feed.» What do piglets do at feeding time? | *Drink their mother's milk | Sleep high up in a tree | Throw heavy metal balls | Dig up roots with their snouts
test: «Piglet was nervous, but he still helped Pooh.» What is Piglet here? | A sunny campsite | A wild boar | *A character, Pooh's small friend | A farm shed
exam: What does piglet mean in «A sow with eight piglets fed them all day»? | Pink | A tiny wooden ball | *A baby pig | Lost
